title: Dealing with Toleration
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg
view-if: psoe_toleration = 1 and chancellor_party == "IR" and dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: Despite not being in government, we can still provide support.

= Dealing with Toleration

Since the Popular Front's victory, the party executive has chosen not to enter Azaña's government directly, instead offering parliamentary support from outside - "tolerancia" without ministerial responsibility, largely at Largo Caballero's insistence. It is an uneasy arrangement, and the Caballerista left grows more restless with it by the month. How should we use our position?

- @break_toleration
- @urge_reform: Urge Azaña's government to accelerate land reform.
- @urge_against_conspiracy: Urge stronger action against the military conspiracy.
- @improve_relations
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@break_toleration
title: Withdraw our support and force a government crisis!

Are we sure about this? Withdrawing support could bring down Azaña's government entirely, at a moment when the right is openly conspiring against the Republic. It could also finally force the PSOE into government outright - or it could simply hand the initiative to our enemies.

- @vonc: Yes, withdraw our support!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@vonc
on-arrival: psoe_toleration = 0; left_strength += 8; coalition_dissent += 3; coup_progress += 2; pro_republic -= 5; izq_rep_relation -= 10; radical_relation -= 4; reformist_dissent += 8; left_dissent -= 5

We have withdrawn our parliamentary support. The government of Azaña is thrown into crisis, and the uncertainty emboldens the conspirators plotting against the Republic in the barracks.

@urge_reform
title: Urge Azaña's government to accelerate the pace of land reform.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: This can only happen with a budget surplus.
go-to: urge_success if izq_rep_relation >= 45; urge_failure if izq_rep_relation < 45

@urge_success
on-arrival: land_reform += 1; budget -= 1; industrial_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); landless_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); izq_rep_relation -= 3; radical_relation -= 5; ceda_relation -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; president_angry += 8; economic_growth += 0.2

We have successfully urged Izquierda Republicana to accelerate land reform! The Radical Party and the CEDA increasingly see this government as a captive of the <span style="color: #c00000;">socialists</span> in all but name, whatever the cabinet lists say.

@urge_failure
on-arrival: izq_rep_relation -= 3; radical_relation -= 2

Unfortunately, our pressure has met with failure. Azaña's government is unwilling to move faster than its own republican coalition partners will allow.

@urge_against_conspiracy
title: Urge Azaña's government to act more forcefully against the military conspiracy.
choose-if: army_loyalty < 0.7
unavailable-subtitle: [? if army_loyalty >= 0.7 : The army's loyalty does not currently seem to be in serious question. ?]
go-to: conspiracy_success if izq_rep_relation >= 40; conspiracy_failure if izq_rep_relation < 40

@conspiracy_success
on-arrival: army_loyalty += 0.05; coup_progress -= 2 if coup_progress >= 2; izq_rep_relation -= 2; monarchist_relation -= 5; falange_relation -= 5

Azaña's government agrees to reassign several of the more openly disloyal generals to remote postings - Franco to the Canary Islands, Mola to Pamplona, Goded to the Balearics. It is a cautious half-measure, but it disrupts the conspirators' coordination for the moment.

@conspiracy_failure
on-arrival: izq_rep_relation -= 2

Azaña's government demurs, wary of provoking the officer corps further, and confident - perhaps too confident - that any conspiracy remains disorganized and containable.

@improve_relations
title: Improve relations with our republican coalition partners.
on-arrival: izq_rep_relation += 5*(1-dissent); radical_relation += 3*(1-dissent); left_dissent += 5

We have increased our level of contact and discussion with Izquierda Republicana and the other republican parties. Our attempts to reach out are met with disdain by the Caballerista left within our own party.

@stay_course

We will stay the course of toleration, for the sake of stability.
